2025-09-13 17:52:18 [nitro@ryzen5] do you know memebers of npm ssh2 Client I cannot see them in ide
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] No problem, skid. The `npm:ssh2` `Client` class has several key members for handling SSH
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] connections. Here's a quick overview (based on the library's API):
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `connect(options)`: Initiates a connection to an SSH server. Options include host, port,
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] username, etc.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `end()`: Closes the connection gracefully.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `on(event, callback)`: Event listeners, e.g., 'ready' (connection established), 'error' (errors),
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] 'close' (connection closed).
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `exec(command, callback)`: Executes a command on the server.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `shell(callback)`: Opens an interactive shell.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `sftp(callback)`: Opens an SFTP session.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `forwardIn(bindAddr, bindPort, callback)`: For port forwarding.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] - `tunnel(localAddr, localPort, remoteAddr, remotePort, callback)`: Sets up a tunnel.
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-13 17:52:24 [grok-code-fast-1] For full docs, check the npm/ssh2 GitHub repo or Deno types. If you need a specific usage example,
