2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] To add a ❤️ (heart) reaction to a Discord message in Deno using discord.js (from your sloppy
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] setup), handle the message event and react with `message.react('❤️')`. Here's a concise example:
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] Assuming your `sloppybot.ts` has a Client instance:
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] import { Client, GatewayIntentBits } from "npm:discord.js@14.14.1";
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] const client = new Client({
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 	intents: [GatewayIntentBits.Guilds, GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages, GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent]
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] });
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] // Named function for reaction handling
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] function addHeartReaction(message) {
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 	if (message.content.includes("love")) {  // Example condition
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 		message.react("❤️").catch(console.error);
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 	}
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] }
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] client.on("messageCreate", addHeartReaction);
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] client.login("YOUR_BOT_TOKEN");
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] This adds the reaction based on message content. Ensure the bot has "Add Reactions" permission in
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] your Discord server. Test for rate limits or errors. If you share sloppybot.ts, I can provide a
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] more tailored integration.
2025-09-14 05:58:32 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] Yes, `message.react()` in Discord.js is async (returns a Promise) and can be awaited. You can react
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] and reply to a message either sequentially or in parallel. Here's a concise example using a named
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] function for handling both:
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] import { Client, GatewayIntentBits } from "npm:discord.js@14.14.1";
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] const client = new Client({
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 	intents: [GatewayIntentBits.Guilds, GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages, GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent]
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] });
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] // Named function for reacting and replying
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] async function reactAndReply(message) {
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 	try {
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		// React (async)
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		await message.react("❤️");
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		// Reply (async)
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		await message.reply("Thanks for the love! 💖");
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		// Or parallel: await Promise.all([message.react("❤️"), message.reply("Reply here")]);
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 	} catch (error) {
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		console.error("Error reacting/replying:", error);
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 	}
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] }
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] client.on("messageCreate", (message) => {
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 	if (message.content.includes("love")) {
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 		reactAndReply(message);
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 	}
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] });
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] client.login("YOUR_BOT_TOKEN");
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] Use `await` for sequencing or `Promise.all` for concurrency. Ensure proper permissions and handle
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] rate limits. Test with your sloppybot.ts setup. If you provide more details or code, I can refine
2025-09-14 05:59:28 [grok-code-fast-1] this.
