2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] Quick assessment (based on the files you shared)
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] - Ingress sources
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Discord: accepts slash/text commands and blobs (no strong auth beyond bot identity). Commands
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] like /commit, /share, /model are actionable.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - SSH: server currently accepts any password auth (context.accept()) — effectively
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] unauthenticated.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Local TCP (fountain/slop): plaintext TCP on port 8081 for messages between components.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - STDIN: local console/system messages accepted.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] - Egress sinks
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Model APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, DeepSeek): sensitive data and files get sent to external
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] LLMs.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Broadcasts to clients (slop/discord/ssh) and file writes to forge directory (shared files
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] persisted).
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - TTS/audio saved to disk and opened.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] - Problem highlights
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - SSH authentication bypass — critical: anyone who can connect to SSH port can act as a session
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] user.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Commands from Discord appear to be trusted to run potentially destructive operations.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Plaintext TCP channel (localhost only today) has no authentication/handshake; if exposed it’s
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] dangerous.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Files uploaded/shared are forwarded to LLMs (and stored) with no content scanning or strong
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] size/type enforcement.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Model switching (/model) and tooling toggle are available from remote clients.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - Deno permissions and environment variables (API keys) are broad; accidental misuse could leak
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] secrets.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - No confirmation step for destructive commands (reset, drop, commit) when invoked remotely.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini]   - No rate limiting, no per-user audit/ACLs visible.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] 
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] High-impact mitigations (prioritise these)
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] - Fix SSH auth immediately: require public-key auth or validate passwords against a whitelist/hash.
2025-09-16 09:23:10 [gpt-5-mini] Do NOT accept all passwords.
