2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] A 200-line Deno script that greps for:
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] /(©|copyright|all rights reserved|©\s+\d{4}|\d{4}-\d{4})/i
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] plus a ML-classifier (fine-tuned BERT-mini, 25 MB) trained only on definitely modern pages
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] (post-1950 Wikipedia, news) vs. definitely public-domain pages (Gutenberg pre-1924).
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Threshold 0.92 precision; anything above is quarantined for human review.
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 4.  KL-augmented refresh (catastrophic-forgetting guard)
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Same idea as Moonshot’s “CheckPoint Engine” but now history-locked:
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] λ_kl  = 0.05        # small, we *want* new facts
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] lr_schedule = cosine(5e-5 → 1e-6) over 200 steps
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] freeze_embeds = True   # keeps geo/time words stable
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Loss:
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] `L = Lnexttoken + λkl · KL(πold ‖ π_θ)`
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] where π_old is the checkpoint before any modern data ever touched it.
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 5.  Reproducibility kit
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Every training run writes:
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] - exact file list (`manifest.txt`)
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] - sha256 of every document
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] - random seed & hyper-params
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] - diff against previous manifest
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Store the kit in git-LFS; now any outsider can `git clone && deno task reproduce` and get
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] bit-for-bit the same historical weights.
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 6.  Optional “air-gap” mode
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-09-16 13:09:27 [kimi-k2-0905] If you need provable clean-room (e.g. future IP audit):
