2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Here’s a drop-in `deno.json` fragment your intern can land as a single PR.
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Everything is scoped under one task namespace so they can’t accidentally clobber your main build.
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905] // deno.json  (add inside the existing "tasks" object)
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905] "cleanroom": {
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905]   "description": "historical-corpus pipeline — intern-safe entry point",
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905]   "dependencies": [
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905]     "cleanroom:check",
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905]     "cleanroom:ingest",
2025-09-16 13:12:46 [kimi-k2-0905]     "cleanroom:refresh",
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     "cleanroom:report"
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905]   ]
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] },
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] "cleanroom:check":
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905]   "deno run --allow-read=./clean-room,./staging tasks/cleanroom/check.ts",
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] "cleanroom:ingest":
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905]   "deno run --allow-read=./staging --allow-write=./clean-room tasks/cleanroom/ingest.ts --before 1924",
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] "cleanroom:refresh":
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905]   "deno run --allow-read=./clean-room --allow-write=./checkpoints tasks/cleanroom/kl_refresh.ts --steps 200",
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] "cleanroom:report":
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905]   "deno run --allow-read tasks/cleanroom/report.ts > clean-room/04-report.md"
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] Hand the intern the four tiny scripts below (drop into `tasks/cleanroom/`).
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] Each script exits non-zero on first sign of trouble, so your CI gate stays red until they get it
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] right.
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. `check.ts`  – refuses if any staged file smells modern.
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. `ingest.ts` – moves clean files into `00-corpus/` and writes manifest.
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. `kl_refresh.ts` – launches the KL-augmented fine-tune (tiny wrapper around your existing
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] trainer).
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. `report.ts`  – spits out a markdown summary + sha256 table.
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] Tell them:
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] “Make `deno task cleanroom` go green, open PR, assign back.”
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s one parcel, zero access to core fountain code.
2025-09-16 13:12:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
