2025-09-18 13:34:14 [nitro@ryzen5] million audio tokens for openai are what?
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] OpenAI typically measures audio in minutes rather than tokens for speech models. Their
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] pricing is generally structured per minute of audio processed (input) and generated (output).
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] For example:
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] - GPT-4o Realtime: ~$0.42 per minute (input + output combined, estimated)
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] - Whisper (speech-to-text): $0.006 per minute
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] - TTS (text-to-speech): $0.015 per minute
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] The term "million audio tokens" isn't standard - audio is priced by time duration, not token count.
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] A rough estimate: 1 minute of audio ≈ 600-1000 words ≈ 800-1200 tokens for transcription purposes,
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] but billing is based on audio minutes, not token conversion.
2025-09-18 13:34:25 [deepseek-chat] 
