2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] • Key points:*
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] - The `responses` endpoint expects `input` to be a string, not a messages array
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] - You'll need to implement a `responses.create()` method in your OpenAI endpoint handler
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] - The response format will be different - it returns a simpler structure with just the generated
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] text
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] The `payload.messages` array contains objects with `role` and `content` properties, so you need to
2025-09-24 08:09:51 [deepseek-chat] convert it to a single string for the responses endpoint.
