2025-09-24 09:19:49 [nitro@ryzen5] sorry i mean which is best practise, npm: or jsr: ?
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] For Deno projects, JSR is the better practice when available.
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] • JSR advantages:*
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - Designed specifically for Deno/TypeScript
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - Type-safe by default
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - Better tree-shaking
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - Deno-first ecosystem
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] • Use npm: when:*
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - Package isn't available on JSR
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - You need specific npm-only packages
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] - Working with legacy code
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] • Best practice:* Prefer JSR packages, fall back to npm: when necessary. Many popular
2025-09-24 09:19:58 [deepseek-chat] packages are now available on both.
