2025-09-25 07:31:19 [nitro@ryzen5] I NEED to tidy current projects
2025-09-25 07:31:32 [nitro@ryzen5] but a solid plan wouldnt hurt
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] Here’s a four-phase “tidy-and-finish” plan you can adapt for any of your Hackaday-style builds:
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 1. Discover & Audit
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• List every active project (VIC-20↔PS1 bridge, Pico hub, cart firmware, etc.)
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Note current status, blockers, next obvious step
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Gather all related files (code repos, schematics, BOMs, breadboard photos)
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 2. Prioritize & Scope
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Assign each project a priority (P1 = must-finish; P2 = nice-to; P3 = archive)
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Define “done” for P1 items (e.g. basic byte-bridge working end-to-end)
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Break each “done” into 2–5 milestones with clear deliverables
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 3. Organize & Execute
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Repo structure
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025]   – 1 folder per project, with README.md, /src, /docs, /hw
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025]   – Tag releases (v0.1, v1.0) as you hit milestones
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Task tracking
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025]   – Lightweight Kanban (Trello/Notion/GitHub Issues)
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025]   – “To do” → “In progress” → “Verify” → “Done”
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Physical tidy
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025]   – Label cables, PCBs and modules
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025]   – Store BOMs and parts in labeled bins
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 4. Review & Close
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Weekly 15-min “stand-up”: check off tasks, re-prioritize
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Finalize documentation: wiring diagrams, usage notes, example code
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Publish: blog post, GitHub release, Hackaday.io project page
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 	• Archive P2/P3 in a “Parked Projects” folder for future revival
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] Once you’ve got P1 items across the finish line, you’ll have a clean workspace, clear repos, and a
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] repeatable workflow for all your retro-hardware hacks.
2025-09-25 07:31:43 [o4-mini-2025] 
