2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] Sounds good. You already get a console message whenever commitShares spots a new, updated or
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] removed file. If you want to “style” those notices you can:
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] • Add an optional style field to each share object
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] • In commitShares wrap your echo calls with ansiStyle(), e.g.
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025]     echo(ansiStyle(`New share: ${path}`, “underline”, 2))
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] 
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] That way new or changed shares pop in bold/underline or your chosen color. Let me know if you’d
2025-09-25 07:50:36 [o4-mini-2025] like a short code snippet.
