2025-09-29 10:40:17 [deepseek-chat] - Can expand while volume is in use
2025-09-29 10:40:17 [deepseek-chat] - Resize in AWS Console or CLI
2025-09-29 10:40:17 [deepseek-chat] - May require OS-level expansion (resize filesystem)
2025-09-29 10:40:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:40:17 [deepseek-chat] The price increase is linear with storage size for gp3 volumes.
2025-09-29 10:40:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:03 [nitro@ryzen5] measure size of folder recusrively in linunx cli
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] Use `du` (disk usage) command:
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] du -sh /path/to/folder
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Common options:*
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - `-s` - show total for folder only (not subfolders)
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - `-h` - human readable (KB, MB, GB)
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - `-c` - show total at the end
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - `--max-depth=N` - limit recursion depth
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Examples:*
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] du -sh /home/user/documents    # Total size only
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] du -h --max-depth=1 /var/log  # Size of top-level folders
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] du -sh *                      # All items in current directory
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:44:59 [nitro@ryzen5] in ec2 dashboard, can i enlarge gp3 type storage?
