2025-09-29 10:48:41 [nitro@ryzen5] scp recurive to another host
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] To copy files and directories recursively to another host using SCP:
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] scp -r /path/to/local/directory username@remote_host:/path/to/destination/
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] • Key points:*
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] - `-r` flag enables recursive copying
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] - Replace paths and credentials with your actual values
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] - You'll be prompted for the remote user's password
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] Example:
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] scp -r ./my_project user@192.168.1.100:/home/user/backups/
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] This will copy the entire `my_project` directory and all its contents to the remote host.
2025-09-29 10:48:48 [deepseek-chat] 
