2025-09-29 10:50:41 [nitro@ryzen5] scp says no space left on device?
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] The "no space left on device" error means the destination disk is full.
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] • Quick solutions:*
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 1. Check disk space on destination:
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] df -h
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 2. Free up space:
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] - Delete unnecessary files
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] - Clear logs: `sudo journalctl --vacuum-size=100M`
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] - Remove old packages: `sudo apt autoremove` (Ubuntu/Debian)
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 3. Copy only essential files instead of the entire directory
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 4. Use rsync with compression if bandwidth is limited:
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] rsync -avz /local/path/ user@host:/destination/
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] Check which partition is full and clean up space before retrying SCP.
2025-09-29 10:50:49 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:08 [nitro@ryzen5] plenty of room,
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] If there's plenty of disk space but SCP still reports "no space left on device," try these
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] solutions:
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 1. Check inode usage:
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] df -i
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] (Even with free space, you can run out of inodes)
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 2. Temp directory might be full:
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] - Check `/tmp` space
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] - Set a different temp dir: `export TMPDIR=/path/with/space`
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 3. Use rsync instead:
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] rsync -avP /local/path/ user@host:/destination/
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 4. Try SCP with different options:
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] scp -r -o IPQoS=throughput /path/ user@host:/destination/
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] The `-P` flag in rsync shows progress and might reveal more specific errors.
2025-09-29 10:51:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:17 [nitro@ryzen5] amazon linux 2 swap space
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] To check and manage swap space on Amazon Linux 2:
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] • Check current swap:*
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] sudo swapon --show
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] free -h
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] • Create swap file:*
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] sudo dd if=/dev/zero of=/swapfile bs=128M count=8
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] sudo chmod 600 /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:43:25 [deepseek-chat] sudo mkswap /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] sudo swapon /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] • Make permanent:*
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] Add to `/etc/fstab`:
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] /swapfile swap swap defaults 0 0
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] • Remove swap:*
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] sudo swapoff /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] sudo rm /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] Adjust `bs` and `count` values for desired swap size (128M × 8 = 1GB in example).
2025-09-29 11:43:26 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:08 [nitro@ryzen5] dd: memory exhausted by input buffer of size 8589934592 bytes (8.0 GiB)
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] The error means `dd` is trying to allocate too much memory at once. Use smaller block sizes:
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] • Better approach for Amazon Linux 2:*
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo fallocate -l 1G /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo chmod 600 /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo mkswap /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo swapon /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] • If fallocate isn't available:*
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo dd if=/dev/zero of=/swapfile bs=1M count=1024 status=progress
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo chmod 600 /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo mkswap /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo swapon /swapfile
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] • Smaller blocks if needed:*
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] sudo dd if=/dev/zero of=/swapfile bs=64M count=16 status=progress
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] The `fallocate` method is fastest and doesn't have the memory issue.
2025-09-29 11:45:18 [deepseek-chat] 
