2025-09-30 08:26:31 [nitro@ryzen5] export keypair from aws console?
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] You cannot directly export the private key of an existing AWS key pair through the AWS Console.
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] However, here are your options:
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] • For NEW key pairs:*
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] - When creating a new key pair in EC2, you can download the .pem file (private key) immediately
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] - This is your only chance to get the private key
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] • For EXISTING key pairs:*
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] - You cannot retrieve the private key if you didn't save it initially
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] - You'll need to create a new key pair and associate it with your instances
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] - Consider using AWS Systems Manager Session Manager as a keyless alternative
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] • Alternative approach:*
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] - Use AWS CLI: Create new key pair and save private key
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] aws ec2 create-key-pair --key-name MyKeyPair --query 'KeyMaterial' --output text > MyKeyPair.pem
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] Would you like help with key pair rotation or alternative access methods?
2025-09-30 08:26:40 [deepseek-chat] 
