2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] Yes, based on the provided files, the system supports recording of PCM (Pulse Code Modulation)
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] audio packets, and these can be stored as part of an event "clip".
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] 
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] 1.  PCM Recording:
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash]     *   The `dspmeter.js` component, when its "Emit" toggle is active, captures audio input (e.g.,
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] from a microphone) via an `AudioWorklet` (`NitroSpectrumProcessor`). This raw PCM data is then
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] packaged as `pcm` events and pushed into the `LocalEventQueueMessage`.
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash]     *   The `nitro-vsynth.js` component, specifically the `VSynthNode` (triggered by the Synth
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] tab's "Record" toggle, which maps to MIDI CC 44), can capture its own mixed audio output (synth
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] sounds plus any `pcm` input streams). This captured output is sent back to the main thread as
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] `vsynth` events, also via `LocalEventQueueMessage`.
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash]     *   Both `pcm` and `vsynth` events are then appended to the `LocalEventRecording` array in
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] `dsptool.js` when recording is active. The `ClipRecording()` function can then retrieve and clear
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] this array, and `addClip()` can store it in `soundClips`.
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] 
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] 2.  PCM Playback:
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash]        The current `PlayClip()` function in `dsptool.js` (which calls `playEvent`) is primarily
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] designed to play back MIDI events from a recorded clip by routing them to the local synth
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] (`synthLocal.onMidi`). It does not currently contain specific logic to directly play back the
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] recorded PCM audio data* (from `pcm` or `vsynth` events) stored within those clips.
2025-10-09 17:23:21 [gemini-2.5-flash] 
