2025-10-10 12:06:14 [gemini-2.5-flash] It appears there's some confusion due to `sloppybot.ts` running in interactive mode while also
2025-10-10 12:06:14 [gemini-2.5-flash] relaying Discord messages.
2025-10-10 12:06:14 [gemini-2.5-flash] 
2025-10-10 12:06:14 [gemini-2.5-flash] 1.  Interactive Mode & Discord: `sloppybot.ts` acts as a bridge. When you type in the
2025-10-10 12:06:14 [gemini-2.5-flash] terminal where `sloppybot.ts` is running, that input is sent to `fountain.ts`. Simultaneously,
2025-10-10 12:06:14 [gemini-2.5-flash] messages from Discord are also sent to `fountain.ts` via `sloppybot.ts`. This can indeed be
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] confusing, as your direct terminal input gets mixed with Discord traffic.
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] 2.  Connection Refused: The `[FEEP]` error indicates `sloppybot.ts` initially couldn't
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] connect to `fountain.ts` on `localhost:8081`. Ensure `fountain.ts` is running before
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] starting `sloppybot.ts`. The later `[BOT] connected` suggests a successful retry or restart of
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] `sloppybot.ts`.
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] 3.  Shared Files/Cleanup: These messages (`Feel free to comment if shared files are new or
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] different.`, `cleanupRequired`) are coming from `fountain.ts`. They appear after `/share` or
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] `/commit` commands are processed. If you've shared many files, you can manage them within
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] `fountain.ts` using commands like `/drop` (to remove from the current session's shared list) or
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] `/reset` (to reset the session entirely, including shared files and history).
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] 
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] To avoid confusion, it's recommended to run `fountain.ts` and `sloppybot.ts` in separate terminal
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] windows. You would interact with `fountain.ts` directly in its terminal, and with `sloppybot.ts`
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] via Discord.
2025-10-10 12:06:15 [gemini-2.5-flash] 
