2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] • Pros:*
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - Consistent experimentation (you want all models at 0.7 for comparison)
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - Simple `/temp` command interface
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - Matches research use case - testing same parameters across providers
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] • Cons:*
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - Different models have different "sweet spots" (Claude likes 0.3-0.7, GPT-4o works well at
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 0.2-1.0, Gemini varies)
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - No model-specific optimization
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - Switching models doesn't adapt temperature automatically
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] Per-Model/Persona Approach 🧠 Better for Production
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] Option 1: Model Defaults in `modelSpecs.json`
