2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] Option 2: Persona Class 🎭 Most Flexible
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] class ModelPersona {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     constructor(
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         public name: string,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         public model: string,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         public temperature: number = 0.7,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         public tools: boolean = true,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         public maxTokens: number = 2048,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         public thinkingBudget?: number
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     ) {}
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     toPayload(): any {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         return {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]             model: this.model,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]             temperature: this.temperature,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]             max_tokens: this.maxTokens,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]             tools: this.tools ? rohaTools : undefined,
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]             config: this.thinkingBudget ? { thinkingConfig: { thinkingBudget: this.thinkingBudget } } : undefined
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         };
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     }
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] }
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] // Usage:
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] const personas = {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     "researcher": new ModelPersona("Researcher", "gpt-4o@openai", 0.3, true, 4096, 1024),
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     "creative": new ModelPersona("Creative", "claude-3-5-sonnet@anthropic", 0.8, false, 2048),
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     "budget": new ModelPersona("Budget", "deepseek-chat@deepseek", 0.5, true, 1024)
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] };
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] let currentPersona = personas.researcher;
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] // In relay():
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] payload = { ...currentPersona.toPayload(), messages: strictHistory(rohaHistory) };
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] Option 3: Hybrid (Recommended) 🔄
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] Keep global temperature but add model overrides:
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] // Global still exists for manual control
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] let grokTemperature = 0.7;
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] // But models can override
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] function getEffectiveTemperature(modelname: string): number {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     const spec = modelSpecs[modelname];
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     if (spec && spec.default_temp !== undefined && !spec.cold) {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]         return spec.default_temp;
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     }
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     return grokTemperature;  // Fall back to global
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] }
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] // In relay():
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] const effectiveTemp = getEffectiveTemperature(payload.model);
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] if (effectiveTemp !== undefined && !info.cold) {
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     payload.temperature = effectiveTemp;
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non]     echoStatus(`[TEMP] ${payload.model}: ${effectiveTemp.toFixed(1)}°`);
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] }
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] My Recommendation: Hybrid Approach
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 1. Keep global temperature for your research workflow (`/temp` command)
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 2. Add `default_temp` to `modelSpecs.json` for model-specific optimization
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 3. Use `getEffectiveTemperature()` to choose between global and model default
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 4. Display which one was used in status (global vs model-specific)
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] This gives you:
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - ✅ Current simple workflow preserved
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - ✅ Automatic optimization when switching models
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - ✅ Clear feedback about which temperature is active
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] - ✅ Easy experimentation (global overrides model defaults)
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] • Implementation:*
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
