2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] const effectiveTemp = getEffectiveTemperature(modelname);
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] const tempSource = spec?.default_temp ? "model" : "global";
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] echo_row(..., `${effectiveTemp.toFixed(1)}°(${tempSource})`);
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] // Status bar:
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] const effectiveTemp = getEffectiveTemperature(grokModel);
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] const tempDisplay = `${effectiveTemp.toFixed(1)}°`;
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] This way you get the best of both worlds - research consistency with automatic model optimization.
2025-10-11 09:13:08 [grok-4-fast-non] 
