2025-10-11 10:26:02 [nitro@ryzen5] 				if (i + bytesNeeded <= n) {					const sequence=value.subarray(i, i + bytesNeeded);					try {						const char=utfDecoder.decode(sequence);						bytes.push(...utfEncoder.encode(char));						addInput(char);						i += bytesNeeded - 1; // Skip the extra bytes						continue;
2025-10-11 10:26:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes – you can drop the manual `i += …` if you collect the whole sequence first and let the outer
2025-10-11 10:26:27 [kimi-k2-0905] loop advance by one logical character at a time.
