2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] The stack pointer decrements on push in most common architectures (x86, ARM).
2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] Memory is typically allocated "downward," so pushing a value decrements the stack pointer to the
2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] next available lower address.
2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] Your description "recursive push increments the pointer to no return" is technically inverted for
2025-10-21 08:42:44 [deepseek-chat] these systems. A more precise phrasing would be:
