2025-10-21 13:49:29 [kimi-k2-0905] That error means the request you sent to the model is ~15 MB, but the provider caps individual
2025-10-21 13:49:29 [kimi-k2-0905] requests at 4 MB.
2025-10-21 13:49:29 [kimi-k2-0905] The only fix is to make the payload smaller: shorten the prompt, remove large inline files, or
2025-10-21 13:49:29 [kimi-k2-0905] split the job into several smaller calls.
2025-10-21 13:49:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] The 15 MB payload is almost certainly the full source of `slopfountain.ts` (≈ 120 k lines).
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] Nothing in the visible prompt asks for the whole file, so the model is probably echoing it back as
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] “context” or because it mis-parsed an earlier message.
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick fixes you can apply inside Fountain:
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Drop the oversized share before the next turn
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    `/drop`              # removes all attached shares from history
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    or
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    `/reset`             # clears history + shares, keeps the model
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Prevent it happening again
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Only `/share` individual files you really need
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Raise `MaxFileSize` in `slopfountain.ts` if you truly need big files, but stay under the 4 MB
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] wire limit
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Use `/commit <tag>` to attach files only when the model explicitly asks for them
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. If you need the big file later, split it:
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905]    `split -b 3M slopfountain.ts part-`   # produces 3 MB chunks, then share the relevant chunk
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] After `/drop` or `/reset` you can keep chatting; the 400 error will disappear because the request
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] size drops back below 4 MB.
2025-10-21 13:49:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
