2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] Correct—the 4 MB limit applies to the entire request payload (history + attachments + prompt), not
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] individual files.
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] The `MaxFileSize` constant I mentioned only controls when a single file gets rejected
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] during `/share`. It doesn’t directly affect the 4 MB relay limit.
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] To stay under the 4 MB threshold:
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 1. Drop large shares before chatting:
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus]    `/drop`
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 2. Shorten the conversation history if it’s grown too long:
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus]    `/reset`
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 3. Use smaller prompts or split large tasks into multiple requests.
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] The `MaxFileSize` constant is just a pre-filter to prevent huge files from being attached in the
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] first place. The actual relay limit is hardcoded in the API provider (4 MB) and enforced before the
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] request reaches the model.
2025-10-21 13:52:39 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
