2025-10-21 14:01:37 [nitro@ryzen5] there is error with model next and the name is "*"
2025-10-21 14:01:42 [nitro@ryzen5] >/model nextcurrent 98next active model is grok-code-fast-1@xaimodel: {"name":"*","emoji":"��","rate":[0.2,0.02,1.5],"limit":0,"balance":"$10.9840","modelname":"grok-code-fast-1@xai"}
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] There's a bug in the `aboutModel` function. In this line:
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] const name=mut+active?"*":"";
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] The operator precedence is wrong. It should be:
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] const name = mut + (active ? "*" : "");
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] • What's happening:*
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] - `mut+active` concatenates the model name string with the boolean `active` value
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] - This creates a truthy string like `"grok-code-fasttrue"`
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] - The ternary operator then returns `"*"` instead of the intended model name with optional asterisk
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] • The fix:*
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] Change that line to properly parenthesize the conditional expression so it evaluates as `mut +
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] (active ? "*" : "")`.
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] This will correctly show the model name with an asterisk for active models, like
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] `"grok-code-fast*"`.
2025-10-21 14:01:50 [grok-code-fast-1] 
