2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. The raw mode input processing - slopPrompt uses `Deno.stdin.setRaw(true)` which bypasses
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] normal terminal input handling
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. UTF-8 byte sequence processing - the code manually processes bytes and has special
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] handling for multi-byte UTF-8 sequences, but some Unicode characters may not be processed correctly
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Wide character detection - the `stringWidth()` function has specific Unicode ranges for
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] determining character width, and some characters may not be properly categorized
2025-10-21 15:13:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
