2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] The issue is that the function is filtering devices very specifically - it's only looking for USB
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] devices from "Raspberry_Pi" vendor. This would explain why you're getting empty results.
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] The function should be modified to enumerate all available serial/COM ports. Here's what needs to
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] be changed:
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Remove the vendor filter:
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] `udevenumerateaddmatchproperty(it,"IDVENDOR","RaspberryPi");`
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Consider expanding beyond just "tty" subsystem to include other relevant subsystems
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. The current implementation only returns an empty array `[]`
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] The function is designed to return JSON information about available ports, but the current
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] filtering is too restrictive for most systems.
2025-10-21 17:29:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 
