2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] Yes, there are several issues with `processUtf8`:
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 1. Buffer overflow risk - The function modifies the `bytes` array parameter without bounds
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] checking
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 2. Incomplete UTF-8 validation - Only checks first byte, doesn't validate continuation
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] bytes follow `10xxxxxx` pattern
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 3. Missing error handling - Invalid sequences aren't handled gracefully
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 4. Inconsistent logging - Always logs even when decoding fails
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] Here's a safer implementation:
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] function processUtf8(value: Uint8Array, i: number, bytes: number[]): number {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     const byte = value[i];
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     let bytesNeeded = 1;
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     if ((byte & 0xE0) === 0xC0) bytesNeeded = 2;
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     else if ((byte & 0xF0) === 0xE0) bytesNeeded = 3;
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     else if ((byte & 0xF8) === 0xF0) bytesNeeded = 4;
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     if (i + bytesNeeded > value.length) {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         return 0; // Incomplete sequence
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     }
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     // Validate continuation bytes
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     for (let j = 1; j < bytesNeeded; j++) {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         if ((value[i + j] & 0xC0) !== 0x80) {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]             return 0; // Invalid continuation byte
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         }
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     }
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     const sequence = value.subarray(i, i + bytesNeeded);
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     try {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         const charText = decoder.decode(sequence);
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         if (charText) {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]             addInput(charText);
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]             bytes.push(...sequence);
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]             console.log("[RAW] skipping ", bytesNeeded, sequence, charText);
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]             return bytesNeeded - 1;
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         }
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     } catch (e) {
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]         console.log("[RAW] decoder error", e);
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     }
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus]     return 0;
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] }
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] The main issue causing your logs is that invalid UTF-8 sequences are being processed as valid,
2025-10-24 08:38:29 [qwen3-coder-plus] creating the replacement character () sequences you observed.
