2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] The `chcp 65001` command sets Windows console to UTF-8 mode, which is correct. For UTF-16 handling
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] you could try:
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] function processUtf16Fallback(value: Uint8Array, i: number, bytes: number[]): number {
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 	// Check for UTF-16 surrogate pairs (0xD800-0xDFFF)
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 	if (value[i] >= 0xD8 && value[i+1] >= 0x00 && value[i+1] <= 0xFF) {
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 		const high = (value[i] << 8) | value[i+1];
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 		if (0xD800 <= high && high <= 0xDBFF) { // High surrogate
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 			if (i + 3 < value.length) {
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 				const low = (value[i+2] << 8) | value[i+3];
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 				if (0xDC00 <= low && low <= 0xDFFF) { // Low surrogate
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 					const codepoint = 0x10000 + ((high & 0x3FF) << 10) + (low & 0x3FF);
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 					const char = String.fromCodePoint(codepoint);
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 					addInput(char);
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 					bytes.push(...encoder.encode(char));
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 					return 3; // Skip 3 bytes (we're at first of 4)
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 				}
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 			}
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 		}
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 	}
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 	return 0;
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] }
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:06:03 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
