2025-10-24 09:11:42 [nitro@ryzen5] does deno support windows clipboard?
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] Yes, Deno supports Windows clipboard through the `navigator.clipboard` API, but with some
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] limitations.
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] • Current Support:*
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] - Works in Deno Deploy and web contexts
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] - For local Windows clipboard access, you need `--allow-read` and `--allow-write` permissions
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] - Uses system clipboard APIs when available
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] • Example:*
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] // Reading from clipboard
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] const text = await navigator.clipboard.readText();
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] // Writing to clipboard
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] await navigator.clipboard.writeText("Hello, clipboard!");
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] • Note:* On Windows, you may need to install additional dependencies for full clipboard
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] functionality, and behavior can vary between Deno versions. Always test with your specific Deno
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] version and target environment.
2025-10-24 09:11:45 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
