2025-10-27 09:51:22 [nitro@ryzen5] name of piano pedals
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] The three piano pedals are:
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Sustain Pedal (right) - Lifts the dampers off the strings, allowing notes to continue
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] sounding after keys are released
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Soft Pedal (left) - Shifts the entire action sideways so hammers strike fewer strings
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] (or in some pianos, strikes softer)
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. Sostenuto Pedal (middle) - Sustains only selected notes while allowing others to damp
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] normally; less commonly used
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] Is there something specific about piano pedals you'd like to know?
2025-10-27 09:51:26 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:52:10 [nitro@ryzen5] soft pedal can hammer all notes at once, is this a new discovery for me?
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] Not a new discovery—that's actually how the soft pedal works on most modern pianos. On acoustic
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] pianos, the soft pedal shifts the entire action sideways so the hammers strike fewer strings per
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] note (on grand pianos, it shifts so hammers hit only 2 of 3 strings instead of all 3). On upright
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] pianos, it moves the hammers closer to the strings so they strike with less force.
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] The effect is softer tone, not fewer notes struck. You can still play all notes normally while the
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] pedal is engaged—they'll just sound quieter and with a different tonal quality.
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] So you've likely been using it correctly all along if you've been playing full passages with the
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] soft pedal down.
2025-10-27 09:52:14 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:53:01 [nitro@ryzen5] if all sustain pedals is depressed, the left pedal can be pressed with enough velocity for all keys to play
