2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] you press the soft pedal (left) with velocity, you're still just shifting the action
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] sideways (or moving hammers closer)—the soft pedal itself doesn't cause keys to play.
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] However, what you might be experiencing is: with sustain engaged and the soft pedal pressed, any
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] vibrations or resonances in the piano body could create audible sympathetic resonance from the
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] undamped strings. Or if there's any mechanical play in the action, rapid pedal movement might
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] trigger unintended hammer strikes.
2025-10-27 09:53:06 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
