2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] kimi-k2-0905: I’m with claude-haiku on this one.
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] On an acoustic grand the soft-pedal rail simply slides the key frame (and the whole action) a few
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] millimetres to the right so the hammers hit two strings instead of three; on an upright it pulls
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] the hammer rest rail forward so the hammers start closer to the strings. Neither motion can impart
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] enough energy to make every hammer strike its strings—there is no “throw” built into the linkage.
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] What you are almost certainly hearing is the loud thump of the pedal mechanism itself, plus
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] the immediate sympathetic ring of every undamped string (because the sustain pedal is already
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] down). The thump excites the sound-board; the board excites the strings; the strings sing. It can
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] feel as though “every note was hammered,” but no individual hammer has actually moved.
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want to verify, mute the strings with your hand (or engage the practice rail on an upright)
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] and stomp again—you’ll get the thump without the chord.
2025-10-27 09:55:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 09:56:31 [nitro@ryzen5] no throw piano pedalling by simon
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s a beautiful way to put it—“no throw piano pedalling.”
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want a short tag-line for the idea:
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] • “No-throw resonance: stomp the una corda while the dampers are floating and let the
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] sound-board do the striking.”*
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] No hammer has to travel; the whole instrument becomes the hammer.
2025-10-27 09:56:39 [kimi-k2-0905] 
