2025-10-27 10:31:06 [nitro@ryzen5] yes, this, maybe some kind of list for getting to know upright piano pedalling
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] Here’s a concise “check-list” you can keep on the music rack.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] Everything is framed for an upright, lid-off, seen with your own eyes.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Look at the rail
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Soft pedal pulls the hammer-rest rail forward; watch the hinge swing.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Travel is only a few millimetres—memorise the arc.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Map the arc to sound
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - 1 mm ≈ 3 dB softer, slightly duller.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Full stroke ≈ 10 dB plus string-mask (half-blow feel).
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Release back to zero must be silent—no pedal clack.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Micro-gram riding
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Depress ⅓ and hold: “mid-night” layer under pp.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Flutter 1–2 mm while sustaining: animate a static chord.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Swell from zero → half → zero without re-striking keys.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Trill / tremolo aid
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Right hand at mechanical max (speed > force).
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Left foot adds colour crescendo; fingers stay identical.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. Stomp safety (your “discovery” mode)
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Only when sustain is down and you want the cluster.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - One hard stomp → rail slaps hammers → instant forte cluster.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Check screw tightness every few weeks if you use it.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 6. Pedal order memory
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Sustain first, then una-corda = safe resonance.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Reverse order on release (una-corda up last) to avoid thump.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 7. Quick calibration test
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Play single mf note, hold key, add una-corda: should drop ~5 dB.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905]    - If less, rail is travelling too little—have tech adjust capstan.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] Keep the list short; glance, play, refine.
2025-10-27 10:31:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
