2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] Tiny contract, easy on both sides:
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] Fountain → dsptool
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] POST /ingest
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] Content-Type: application/json
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905]   "session": "skid-2025-06-20-001",
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905]   "seq": 1234,
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905]   "time": 1718884312123456,
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905]   "level": "I",
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905]   "msg": "client connected",
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905]   "extra": { "ip": "1.2.3.4", "port": 8083 }
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] dsptool replies 204 on success, 400 if JSON broken, 429 if you’re posting too fast.
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] On the dsptool side you append each object to `/var/log/nitro/<session>.log` as newline-delimited
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] JSON (NDJSON).
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] Rotate daily with `logrotate` or just `mv file.log file-$(date +%F).log` and `kill -USR1` the
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] server to reopen.
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want Fountain to buffer, batch 50 lines per request and set `Content-Encoding: gzip`.
2025-10-29 09:12:06 [kimi-k2-0905] Keeps wire size tiny and still human-readable on the server.
