2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] Why this happens (brief):
2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] - FatSpace is a Unicode space; some terminals/fonts treat it differently next to wide emoji, so the
2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] glyphs butt up visually.
2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Emoji are often double‑width and may join with following characters (or the font may not show the
2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] EM SPACE clearly).
2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] - ANSI/markdown processing or later string trimming could also remove/preserve spaces
2025-10-29 15:25:32 [gpt-5-mini] unpredictably.
