2025-10-29 15:57:39 [nitro@ryzen5] another name for U+FE0E ?
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] Official Unicode name: VARIATION SELECTOR-15 (U+FE0E)
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] 
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] Common aliases
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - VS15
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - text presentation selector
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - “text variant” (contrasts with VS16)
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] 
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] What it does
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - Requests a text/text‑style presentation for the preceding character (where that character has
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] both emoji and text presentations).
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - Counterpart: U+FE0F (VARIATION SELECTOR-16 / VS16) requests emoji presentation.
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] 
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] Code example
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - JS/TS: const bucketText = "🪣\uFE0E"; // bucket forced to text presentation
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] 
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] Notes
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] - Not all fonts/terminals honour it; behavior depends on renderer.
2025-10-29 15:57:50 [gpt-5-mini] 
