2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] The good news: every read_time call actually executed, so the tool-calling loop is working; the bad
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] news: we burned through the 1 M-token/minute limit in ~30 s by firing off 15 rapid-fire requests.
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] Take-aways / quick fixes
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Add a small delay (≥ 2 s) between test calls to stay under 60 requests-per-minute.
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Cache the result locally if you only need one “now” timestamp for a batch of tests.
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Drop back to a cheaper model (gemini-2.0-flash) or a different provider while the quota resets
2025-10-29 16:54:41 [kimi-k2-0905] (≈31 s).
