2025-10-29 16:55:12 [nitro@ryzen5] all the other models called the function once, why is gemini behaving like this?
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] Because the Gemini 2.5 Flash endpoint is streaming the reply token-by-token,
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] and slop-fountain’s relay currently injects every assistant delta into history as soon as it
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] arrives.
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Each delta that contains even a fragment of a `tool_calls` array triggers the same
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] tool-calling logic again, so:
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. First delta → “I see a tool call, run it, push result.”
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Second delta → “Still see a tool call, run it again …”
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. … repeat for every chunk until the stream ends.
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] The other models (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) send the full `tool_calls` list in one
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] non-streaming completion, so the relay only sees the call once.
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick cures (pick one):
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] A. De-duplicate inside `processToolCalls`:
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905]    keep a `Set` of IDs you have already executed and skip duplicates.
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] B. Only run tools on the final chunk (when `finishreason` is `toolcalls`).
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] C. Disable streaming for Gemini (add `stream:false` to the payload when model starts with
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] `gemini`).
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Any of those stops the thundering herd.
2025-10-29 16:55:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:56:56 [nitro@ryzen5] do you think stream false will work? it sounds somplest
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—setting `stream: false` for Gemini is the one-line fix
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] that will stop the duplicate calls immediately.
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] Gemini’s REST endpoint accepts the same parameter as OpenAI; when you switch off streaming you get
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] a single JSON response that contains the complete `tool_calls` array, so the relay sees the call
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] once and life is back to normal.
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick patch (in slopfountain.ts around the Gemini payload builder):
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] if (model.startsWith('models/gemini')) {
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905]   request.stream = false;   // <-- add this
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] (or gate it on `provider === 'gemini'`).
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] No other code changes required, and it keeps the tool-calling logic identical for every provider.
2025-10-29 16:57:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
