2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] again
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] The problem is in how tool calls are being handled in the conversation history. Looking at the code
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] flow:
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] - In `prepareGeminiContent()`, the system is processing all messages including tool calls
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] - When a tool call is processed, the result gets added back to history
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] - But the original tool call message isn't being filtered out properly
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] The fix should be to ensure that when processing tool calls:
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] - Only include the tool results in the conversation history sent to Gemini
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] - Filter out the original tool call messages that triggered the function calls
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] - This prevents the model from seeing its own tool calls as new instructions
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] The key insight is that Gemini is interpreting its own previous tool calls as new requests to make
2025-10-29 17:10:07 [deepseek-chat] more tool calls, creating an infinite loop.
