2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] Gemini's tool calling is designed to be explicit. When you enable tools, Gemini will suggest
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] `functionCalls()` if it believes a tool is relevant. The system then processes these calls
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] sequentially.
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] 
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] To mitigate concerns:
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] • Start with a clean history (`/reset`) when enabling tools to avoid unexpected state from previous
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] interactions.
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] • Monitor the `max_tokens` setting for the model, as this acts as a safeguard against excessive
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] generation.
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] • The `processToolCalls` function in Fountain handles the tool execution and ensures results are
2025-10-29 17:55:34 [gemini-2.5-05] fed back into the conversation, typically preventing infinite loops at that stage.
