2025-10-29 18:11:12 [gemini-2.5-05] `"tool"` consistently after `processToolCalls` allows the model-specific history preparation
2025-10-29 18:11:12 [gemini-2.5-05] functions (like `prepareGeminiContent`, `anthropicMessages`, `plainHistory`, `strictHistory`,
2025-10-29 18:11:12 [gemini-2.5-05] `multiHistory`, `inlineHistory`) to correctly format the tool output for their respective APIs.
2025-10-29 18:11:12 [gemini-2.5-05] 2.  `rohaHistory.push(item);`: Uncommenting this line is crucial. Without it, the results
2025-10-29 18:11:12 [gemini-2.5-05] of the tool calls are never added to the conversation history, meaning the model doesn't receive
2025-10-29 18:11:12 [gemini-2.5-05] the output from the tools it invoked and cannot continue the conversation based on those results.
