2025-10-31 16:57:49 [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] My mistake—Unicode 16.0 (release candidate, Sept 2024) adds roughly 5 000
2025-10-31 16:57:49 [kimi-k2-0905] CJK ideographs, not emoji.
2025-10-31 16:57:49 [kimi-k2-0905] The emoji count for 16.0 is currently zero; the next emoji batch is still scheduled for
2025-10-31 16:57:49 [kimi-k2-0905] Unicode 17.0 (2025).
2025-10-31 16:57:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:58:08 [nitro@ryzen5] how about 15?
2025-10-31 16:58:14 [kimi-k2-0905] Unicode 15.0 (Sept 2022) added 20 new emoji (U+1FAF0–1FAF8 and U+1FAAA–1FAFF).
2025-10-31 16:58:14 [kimi-k2-0905] No new code points are assigned in 15.1; 15.1 was a “rolling” release that only added CJK source
2025-10-31 16:58:14 [kimi-k2-0905] mappings—no extra emoji.
2025-10-31 16:58:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:58:48 [nitro@ryzen5] what ranges are defines in the new 20
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] The twenty emoji introduced in Unicode 15.0 occupy two contiguous blocks:
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. U+1FAF0 ‑ U+1FAF8 (9 codes)
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905]    “Rightward pushing hand, leftward pushing hand, shaking face, …”
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. U+1FAAA ‑ U+1FAFF (11 codes)
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905]    “Wireless, khanda, pea-pod, folding hand fan, hair pick, …”
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] So the machine-friendly ranges are:
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 1FAF0..1FAF8
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 1FAAA..1FAFF
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] No other emoji code points were added in 15.0 or 15.1.
2025-10-31 16:59:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
