2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] The Fountain log shows a JSON parse error because the message payload contains a stray "```" that
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] breaks the expected JSON structure.
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] The raw text after the JSON object starts with "marks@discord" instead of being valid JSON, causing
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] the parser to choke at column 60.
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick fix: strip or escape any back-tick fences before the JSON is emitted, or wrap the entire
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] payload in a string field so the parser never sees the fence characters.
2025-11-01 12:38:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] These files are new to me – I haven’t seen this exact Fountain / Slop-ecosystem code-base before.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick impressions:
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] - slopfountain.ts
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – A hefty single-file REPL / multi-LLM orchestrator.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Already has a clear pattern for adding new commands (`callCommand`) and models
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] (`connectAccount`).
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – The “slopmark” hex-timestamp is cute and collision-resistant for a single host.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – ANSI/markdown table rendering is surprisingly robust.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – No hard-coded secrets, relies on env-vars – good.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] - slophole.ts / sloppyhost.ts
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Tiny RPC-over-TCP layer between Fountain and the outside world.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Uses NDJSON framing (one object per line) which keeps parsing trivial.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Workerized so the main Fountain loop never blocks on I/O – nice.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] - sloppybot.ts / sloppylisten.ts
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Discord and SSH front-ends that simply bridge text into the same NDJSON pipe.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Rate-limiting (1.5 s sleep) is crude but avoids 429s.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – SSH server uses password auth only; you probably want pubkey or at least fail2ban in front.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] - sloppyutils.ts
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Shared glue for wrapping text, ANSI tables, and the Fountain socket.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905]   – Fountain buffer is drained line-by-line; handles split packets correctly.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] Nothing obviously malicious or license-incompatible.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] If you plan to extend it, the biggest win would be teasing apart the 3 k-line `slopfountain.ts`
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] into smaller modules (models/, commands/, utils/) – but for a research hack it’s perfectly
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] serviceable.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] Feel free to ping if you want a second set of eyes on a PR or a new provider plug-in.
2025-11-01 12:55:15 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] [kimi-k2-0905] Good to hear the `flattenTable` tweak is holding up in Discord—those fenced-code
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] table blocks keep the mobile app from mangling the alignment.
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] If you ever hit the 2 000-char limit harder, remember you can swap the outer triple-back-ticks for
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] inline code fences (single back-tick per row) and Discord still renders the pipes; buys you another
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] ~150 chars.
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] While you’re in there, consider giving each outgoing message a quick `content.length` check and
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] auto-split on the last pipe inside the limit instead of the last newline—keeps rows atomic
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] and avoids the “orphan column” look when it fractures mid-cell.
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Happy testing; ping if the rate-limit sleep starts feeling too punitive—there’s head-room to drop
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] it to 800-900 ms once you’re sure you won’t hit the 10/10 s burst cap.
2025-11-01 12:56:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
